{
  "_note": [
    "How the fidelity gate ARRIVES at a screen. One entry per in-scope screen",
    "id: which door, which route, and which login gets there. Extending the",
    "gate to another journey is adding entries here — never editing the gate.",
    "",
    "arrive: 'anon' (no login), 'worker' (#login-grace), 'field' ([data-login]),",
    "or 'console:<persona-key>' (the console's persona card, by data-persona).",
    "route: the hash route inside the door, or '' for the door's entry screen.",
    "",
    "A screen with no entry here is out of the gate's scope and is reported as",
    "such — the gate never silently passes a screen it did not visit."
  ],
  "scope": {
    "journeys": ["p1", "p2"],
    "designScreens": ["n1", "n2", "n3", "n4", "n5"],
    "why": "Phase 1 is scoped to J3 — setting up a project (P-1 Org Admin, P-2 Project Configurator) — plus the five connective-tissue screens our own design adds (docs/design/j3-connective-tissue/README.md)."
  },
  "screens": {
    "p1_1": { "app": "console", "arrive": "console:orgadmin", "route": "#/org" },
    "p1_2": { "app": "console", "arrive": "console:orgadmin", "route": "#/org" },
    "p1_3": { "app": "console", "arrive": "console:orgadmin", "route": "#/org" },

